You'll have to sacrifice BIGGER monsters. The number of creatures
doesn't count: the size and difficulty level does. You can sacrifice
all the newts you like and it'll still be inadequate.

By the way: What race are you? Doppelgangers are considered human, so
if you are human and you sacrificed a doppelganger, you will have
turned the altar Chaotic - which would have angered a co-aligned
Lawful priest, and made him turn against you, because converting an
altar with a priest in attendance will anger the priest.

All these actions (sacrificing your own race when non-chaotic,
converting an altar away from your alignment, and angering and killing
a co-aligned priest) would have been VERY bad for your *alignment* -
the surprise is, when you next sacrificed on that altar (which would
now have been Chaotic), that it must have converted back to YOUR
alignment: under the circumstances, you were far more likely to
convert yourself to Chaotic if you sacrificed on the same altar. So
you've had one lucky escape already, at least (since changing your own
alignment by any means other than a Helm of Opposite Alignment before
completing the Quest makes the game unfinishable.) You must have been
very piously Lawful, so much so that you still had a positive rather
than negative alignment when you did your *next* sacrifice after
killing the priest and desecrating the altar.

(By the way - did you meet and kill a demon lord? Demon lords normally
turn up when you sacrifice your own race: peaceful if you're chaotic,
hostile if you're lawful or neutral.)

Of course, if you're *NOT* human, then sacrificing a doppelganger
should have had no worse effect than sacrificing, say, a kobold...
unless the priest was NOT of the same alignment as you, and you
converted the altar with the sacrifice. Which would have been a good
action, but killing the priest afterwards (or indeed beforehand) is a
bad action: gods don't like it when you anger peaceful priests, even
of a rival god - it sets an unacceptable precedent. Angering a priest,
even one of an opposite alignment, is not a Lawful thing to do: and
the act must have taken your alignment into negative territory, and
then you prayed while you were still in a state of sin, which will
anger your god.

If a god is merely "displeased" (which can happen when your prayer
timeout has not timed out, or if you pray when out of luck), then that
will eventually correct itself over time, or when you bring your luck
back above zero. But if he's "angry" - which can happen if you pray
when you've strayed from your alignment, or if you turn an altar
against you by sacrificing your own race, or if you sacrifice a
co-aligned unicorn on your own altar, or if you sacrifice on Moloch's
altar, or if you pray when your god has already indicated his
displeasure for some other reason - then time will not cure this: you
must make SERIOUS amends, by making a few BIG blood sacrifices to your
god.

